<title>CHINA: China Jan-June edible oil buying detailed.</title>
<headline>China Jan-June edible oil buying detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table shows the three edible oil import figures of five major Chinese customs offices as well as the country of origin in January to June.</p>
<p>Details were provided by the General Administration of Customs of China.</p>
<p>Figures are in tonnes. Percentages represent the share of the total market. Percentages may not add up to 100 because details of some smaller import regions and supplying countries have not been included.</p>
<p>SOYOIL</p>
<p>    June imports  66,274   Jan-June total imports   593,140</p>
<p> CUSTOMS	     June	 Pct	   Jan-June	Pct</p>
<p>    Shanghai	21,021	31.7	  142,593	 24.0</p>
<p>    Huangpu	    307	 0.46	  36,625	  6.2</p>
<p>    Tianjin	    0.0	 0.0	   90,199	 15.2</p>
<p>    Nanjing	    0.0	 0.0	   68,501	 11.5</p>
<p>    Shenzhen	14,198	21.4	   91,013	 15.3</p>
<p>ORIGIN</p>
<p>    Brazil	  40,102	60.5	  264,416	 44.6</p>
<p>    Argentina	  0.0	 0.0	   55,946	  9.4</p>
<p>    U.S.	     6,971	10.5	  209,763	 35.4</p>
<p>    Malaysia	   346	 0.5	   22,095	  3.7</p>
<p>PALM OIL</p>
<p>    June imports   103,887  Jan-June  total imports    458,837</p>
<p> CUSTOMS	     June	 Pct	   Jan-Jun	 Pct</p>
<p>    Shenzhen	 22,438	21.6	   93,471	 20.4</p>
<p>    Shantou	    2273	10.0	   28,964	  6.3</p>
<p>    Nanning	   9,029	 8.7	   28,446	  6.2</p>
<p>    Huangpu	   1,706	 1.6	   31,923	  7.0</p>
<p>    Zhanjiang	 4,515	 4.3	   43,126	  9.4</p>
<p>ORIGIN</p>
<p>    Malaysia	 75,402	72.6	  341,790	 74.5</p>
<p>    Indonesia	22,303	21.5	   97,748	 21.4</p>
<p>RAPESEED OIL</p>
<p>    June imports   18,652   Jan-Jun total imports    150,487</p>
<p> CUSTOMS	     June	 Pct	   Jan-Jun	 Pct</p>
